# Line endings, fixed rather than inherited.
#
# Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: "lf"` and CI runs `format:check` on ubuntu, where
# git checks out LF and the gate passes. On Windows `core.autocrlf` defaults to true, so a
# clean checkout of this same commit arrives with CRLF and `format:check` fails on every
# text file in the repository.
#
# That made the clean-checkout verification meaningless: it was passing because of a local
# git setting rather than because of anything in the tree. Declaring the intent here makes
# the working copy identical on every platform, so the gate tests the commit instead of the
# machine.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binaries; `eol=lf` fixes the checkout for everything it
# decides is text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, named explicitly so nothing depends on heuristics getting them right.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
